# GitHub Copilot Instructions

- Use `uv` for dependency management, virtual environments, and command execution.
- Preserve the layering: `api` (models, schemas, services, dependencies), `core` (config, logging, telemetry), `database` (session, queues, repositories), and `routes`.
- Keep all HTTP handlers asynchronous.
- Use SQLAlchemy ORM with `asyncpg`; do not introduce synchronous database access.
- Add Google-style docstrings with explicit types for attributes, arguments, and returns.
- Prefer dependency injection through `src/{{ package_name }}/bootstrap.py` and `src/{{ package_name }}/api/dependencies.py`.
- Route long-running work through queue adapters instead of blocking request handlers.
- Keep tracing and logging wired through OpenTelemetry-aware helpers in `src/{{ package_name }}/core`.
- Refresh `.agents/skills` and `.claude/skills` with `uv run library-skills --tool-skill install --claude --yes --all` when dependencies change.
